    "explanation": "To both parties — this ruling refunds $4.00 of the $9.00 contested, as a PARTIAL_REFUND. Deviation is established on the trace: EV-GPS-00103 records 11.18 km against the booked optimal of 8.2 km on EV-TRIP-00103, an excess of 2.98 km, 36.34% of optimal, so both POL-RD-01 tests pass (the trace figure governs over the rounded 11.2 km copy, as POL-RD-01 requires). The trace is unimpaired — 175 fixes at a 10-second interval, no gaps, 100% coverage — so POL-RD-07 does not bite and no independent corroboration is needed; every artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02 caps nothing. The diversion is excused. EV-ADVIS-00103-01 (LTA closure of Braddell Road towards Serangoon, 05:30–12:00) names the corridor the optimal route uses and covers the 08:07–08:36 trip. Under POL-RD-03 the justified excess is min(2.98, 1.30 x (10.6 − 8.2) + 1.00) = min(2.98, 4.12) = 2.98 km, so the entire excess is justified and the exoneration is complete. Because an exculpatory clause fully excuses the deviation, POL-RD-02 does not run and the distance and time charges stand. I therefore did not adopt the $4.15 closure figure shown on EV-FARE-00103: POL-RD-02 runs against the closure-adjusted optimal only where some excess is left unexcused, and here none is. The driver's rider-requested-detour submission is rejected. POL-RD-04 requires the instruction to come from the rider and to name a place or road; the only road named ('braddell close today, i take CTE ah') was named by the driver, and the rider's reply 'ok' names nothing. POL-RD-04 is unavailable, POL-RD-09(3) is not engaged, and no ERP refund is forfeited. What is refunded is the off-route ERP. EV-FARE-00103 itemises CTE (Braddell Rd) $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd) $1.00, both on_optimal_route false, against an optimal-route ERP of $0.00 — an off-route total of $4.00, inside POL-RD-09(2)'s $12.00 cap. Under POL-RD-09(2) the distance and time charges stand but the off-route ERP is corrected as a pass-through. Both gantries are genuine crossings (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 40.2 m, within the 250 m match radius), so no phantom line and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. POL-RD-06 produces no referral either: the deviation is not material (2.98 km / 36.34%, below both gates) and deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 553 completed trips. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires — identifiers match, timestamps run forward, the advisory is on file, and the refund is far below both charged_total and the ceiling. Figures used: charged_total $25.12; optimal-route ERP $0.00; off-route ERP $3.00 + $1.00 = $4.00; refund $4.00. The monetary effect is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically."
